From: RustDesk XR fork
Subject: [PATCH] videotoolbox: immediate packets and optional scene-change QP ladder

Complete each H.264/HEVC frame before returning so its packet is not held until later
input (RUSTDESK_VT_SYNC=0 disables). Optionally (RUSTDESK_VT_SCENE_LADDER, e.g.
"46,40,34,30"), when most of the frame changes, encode it at a coarse base QP and the next
frames at decreasing QPs under low-latency rate control, so a soft picture reaches the
client quickly and sharpens over a few frames (RUSTDESK_VT_SCENE_THRESHOLD sets the
changed-sample percentage, default 30). A frame the encoder fails in that mode is dropped
and the next frame is forced to be a key frame.
---
